---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import FaceBlurCamera from '@/components/tools/redact/vision/FaceBlurCamera.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="face-blur-camera" width="wide">
  <FaceBlurCamera client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to use it</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Press Turn on camera and allow the camera. Every face in view is blurred.</li>
      <li>Turn on Keep the largest face to keep your own face sharp when you are nearest the camera.</li>
      <li>Choose blur, pixelate or a solid fill, the shape and the strength.</li>
      <li>Press Record to save a clip, or Open in a window to show the blurred picture in its own window.</li>
      <li>Press Turn off camera when you are done. The browser releases the camera.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Use it in a video call</h2>
    <p>
      A web page cannot add a camera to your computer. Press Open in a window, then share that window in your video call
      app. Picture in picture shows the same picture in a small window that stays on top.
    </p>

    <h2>What runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The faces are found by a small face detection model (230 kB, MIT license) in a model runtime of 15 MB. Both
      download once from this site and are kept in your browser. The model runs in a background thread as often as your
      device allows, and the tool shows how many times per second. A laptop checks 30 to 70 times per second, a phone
      fewer. Recording uses the recorder of your browser, which saves MP4 or WebM.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check that nothing is uploaded</h2>
    <p>
      Open the developer tools of your browser (F12) and select the Network tab before you turn on the camera. You see the
      model files load from this site the first time and no request after that.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Faces far from the camera, seen from the side or in poor light can be missed for a moment. Do a short test before you rely on it.</li>
      <li>When a face moves fast, the blur can lag behind it by a frame.</li>
      <li>Open in a window and Picture in picture need a browser that supports them. Firefox has no picture in picture button for pages.</li>
      <li>The site cannot use your camera unless you allow it. You can take the permission back in the browser settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Related tools</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/blur-faces-in-video">Video Face Blur</a> for recorded videos,
      <a href="/blur-face-in-photo">Blur Face in Photo</a> for photos, and
      <a href="/webcam-test">Webcam Test</a> to check your camera first.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
